---
import Card from "@/components/Card.astro";
---

<div
	class="w-full h-1/2 bgg-red-600 flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-start gap-4 md:py-6">
	<Card>
		<h3 class="text-balance text-2xl font-semibold">What is this?</h3>
		<p class="text-pretty text-neutral-800 2xl:text-lg">
			This is a desktop app for Windows and can toggle the Windows
			proccess named "File Explorer", when you turn off this, the desktop
			and folder system stop running, and depending on your computer, this
			can free up a lot of ram memory and give you more performance.
		</p>
	</Card>

	<Card>
		<h3 class="text-balance text-2xl font-semibold">How is builded?</h3>
		<p class="text-pretty text-neutral-800 2xl:text-lg">
			Is builded with C#, and you can see the code in the repository,
			likewise in the branch "python" and you can see the same code but
			with Python, the code in python is much more friendly :).
		</p>
	</Card>

	<Card>
		<h3 class="text-balance text-2xl font-semibold">
			Why is it positive for <a
				href="https://www.virustotal.com/gui/home/upload"
				target="_blank"
				class="text-blue-600 underline hover:opacity-75 transition-opacity">
				VirusTotal
			</a>?
		</h3>
		<p class="text-pretty text-neutral-800 2xl:text-lg">
			VirusTotal is a very confident website, but in this case, is a false
			positive. If you have any doubts you can see the code in two
			different languages.
		</p>
	</Card>

	<Card>
		<h3 class="text-balance text-2xl font-semibold">Is it bannable?</h3>
		<p class="text-pretty text-neutral-800 2xl:text-lg">
			Of course not, this software only touch a normal windows procces and
			the only advantage you might have is in the performance of the other
			applications.
		</p>
	</Card>
</div>
